⚙️ Installation and Setup

Follow these steps to run the project on your local machine.

1. Prerequisites

Install the following software:

Node.js
MySQL Server or XAMPP
Visual Studio Code
MySQL Workbench or phpMyAdmin (optional)
2. Clone the Repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/Veenagm/online-railway-ticket-res.git


Navigate to the project directory:

bash
cd online-railway-ticket-res

3. Install Dependencies
bash
npm install

4. Configure the Database
Start your MySQL server.
Open MySQL Workbench or phpMyAdmin.
Locate database/schema.sql.
Execute the SQL script.

This creates the railway_db database and the required tables:

trains
bookings

It also inserts sample train records.

5. Configure Environment Variables

Copy .env.example and create a new file named .env in the project root.

Configure your MySQL credentials:

env
PORT=3000
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=
DB_NAME=railway_db


Update the username and password according to your MySQL configuration.

Note: For a default XAMPP MySQL setup, the username is usually root and the password may be blank.

6. Start the Application

Run the following command:

bash
npm start


For development mode:

bash
npm run dev

7. Open the Application

Open your browser and visit:

http://localhost:3000

The Online Railway Ticket Reservation System is now ready to use!

🔌 API Endpoints

The backend provides the following REST API endpoints:

Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/trains	Search available trains
POST	/api/book	Book a railway ticket
GET	/api/booking?pnr=PNR_NUMBER	Retrieve booking details
POST	/api/cancel	Cancel a booking
GET	/api/health	Check server status
Example API Requests

Search Trains

http
GET /api/trains?from=Bengaluru&to=Hubballi&date=2026-12-10


Book a Ticket

http
POST /api/book


Retrieve Booking Details

http
GET /api/booking?pnr=PNR_NUMBER


Cancel a Ticket

http
POST /api/cancel

🗄️ Database

The project uses MySQL as its database management system.

The database contains two main tables:

1. Trains

Stores train information, including:

Train ID
Train number
Train name
Source and destination
Departure and arrival times
Ticket fare
Total seats

2. Bookings

Stores passenger reservation information, including:

PNR number
Train ID
Journey date
Passenger name
Age and gender
Number of seats
Total fare
Booking status
Booking timestamp
